$1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 64 people. Revenue per employee of $22.1M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $4.4M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $121K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Apple Hospitality REIT, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $4.5B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $282M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.11\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn.","Management returns a meaningful 6.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 7.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9139784946236545},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 10.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 23% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","10 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Apple Hospitality REIT (NYSE:APLE) Sets New 52-Week High Following Strong Earnings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/apple-hospitality-reit-nyseaple-sets-new-52-week-high-following-strong-earnings.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794000044.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.923,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Apple Hospitality raises 2026 RevPAR growth outlook to 5.1%-6.1% as October RevPAR tracks ~10% (NYSE:APLE)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668510-apple-hospitality-raises-2026-revpar-growth-outlook-to-5_1-percentminus-6_1-percent-as","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793997446.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Apple Hospitality (APLE) Q3 2026 Ea